  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Energy Governance and Information System for West Africa (REGIS WA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;To contribute to the overall objective and specific objective 1, the project will support ECOWAS through the implementation of two components:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 1 -&lt;/strong&gt; Support for the implementation and monitoring/follow-up of the regional energy policy, for the transposition in the Member States of the regional directives and the regional energy action plan, and for liaison with the African Union (AU). &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 2 -&lt;/strong&gt; Support for the development of ECOWAS&#xbf;s energy statistical system. Improvement of capacities and support to Member States for the collection and production of statistical energy data, monitoring of the collection and production of statistical data, provision of equipment, software and trainings at the level of ECOWAS and its Member States, strengthening collaboration with African Energy Commission (AFREC&lt;a href=&quot;#_ftn1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt;) on energy statistics, and integrating a gender-sensitive approach where possible. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;#_ftnref1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt; AFREC operates under the African Union, whose main headquarters are in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, but AFREC itself is based in Algiers&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
